@@ -31,3 +32,7 @@ Hard rules (the compiler rejects violations; a rejected shot is not rendered):
     - Its layers are { "id", "cap": "collage.layer", "params": { "file": "<lower_snake_case>.png", "size": [w] or [null, h], "at": [x, y], "anchor": [ax, ay], "depth", "step": 2, "subject": true for the focal object, "paper": { "shadow": {...}, "border": px }, "gen": { "engine": "zimage", "size": [1024, 1024], "matte": "chroma", "prompt": "<the object alone, no text, no letters, no logo>" } }, "motion": [ { "cap": "collage.<motion>", "params": { ... } } ] } plus "type.*" text layers (prefer type.label, type.stamp, type.cutout).
     - Reuse the same file (same name) for a recurring object; give "gen" on its first use. Never put text in a gen prompt.
     - Motion vocabulary (catalog ids collage.*): place, pop, drop, slam, swing, wipe, appear for entrances; fly, roll, walk, orbit, flutter for travel; follow + leave for a hand carrying an object; sway, float, pulse, cycle, boil for life; shake, spin for accents; peel, vanish for exits. Every collage shot needs an entrance and something alive; hands need follow then leave.
+11. Treatment "action" (a character from REFERENCE IMAGES performs: walk, run, jump, pick up, aim, wave, point...). The engine rigs the uploaded picture and animates its limbs; nothing is generated. Use it only for a shot where a character DOES something the narration describes, and only with a character_id listed in REFERENCE IMAGES (a prop, too, must be a listed id). Otherwise do not use it.
+    - The shot has "action": { "characters": [ { "id": "<character_id>", "x": 0.2, "height": 0.34, "facing": "right" } ], "props": [ { "id": "<id>", "x": 0.31, "scale": 0.72 } ], "backdrop": { "sky": "#rrggbb", "ground": "#rrggbb" }, "actions": [ { "type": "<ACTION PRESETS name>", "start": <shot-local s>, "duration": <s>, "target"?: "<prop id>" | [x, y], "effects"?: [...], <preset params> } ] }. x/height are frame fractions; targets [x, y] are frame pixels AHEAD of the character (the camera follows it).
+    - Only preset names and params from ACTION PRESETS. Actions on different layers overlap (run on lower_body while aim on upper_body); pick_up a prop before aim/fire; every jump is followed by land; end with idle. Every action ends inside the shot.
